From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cfg80211: report scan aborts and failures

cntl_scan_conf() discards its MLME status and always reports a successful
scan to cfg80211. Aborted scans therefore produce NEW_SCAN_RESULTS and
can trigger BSS cache expiration for NL80211_SCAN_FLAG_FLUSH requests.

Completion now sets aborted for non-success MLME status and state-machine
resets. Using the status argument preserves the result after channel
restoration clears opAbortScan.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt_wifi/common/fsm/fsm_cntl.c
+++ b/mt_wifi/common/fsm/fsm_cntl.c
@@ -651,7 +651,7 @@ full_reset:
 
 	mark_scan_end_on_wdev(pAd);
 #ifdef APCLI_CFG80211_SUPPORT
-	RT_CFG80211_SCAN_END(pAd, FALSE);
+	RT_CFG80211_SCAN_END(pAd, status != MLME_SUCCESS);
 #endif /* APCLI_CFG80211_SUPPORT */
 
 	return TRUE;
--- a/mt_wifi/common/mlme.c
+++ b/mt_wifi/common/mlme.c
@@ -5798,7 +5798,7 @@ VOID MlmeRestartStateMachine(RTMP_ADAPTE
 #endif /* CONFIG_STA_SUPPORT */
 	/* CFG_TODO for SCAN */
 #ifdef RT_CFG80211_SUPPORT
-	RT_CFG80211_SCAN_END(pAd, FALSE);
+	RT_CFG80211_SCAN_END(pAd, TRUE);
 #endif /* RT_CFG80211_SUPPORT */
 }
 
